\section*{Implementation Notes (Phase 4--5)}

The conceptual diagrams above represent the original design intent from Phase 2. During Phase 4 implementation, several architectural pivots were made in response to ecosystem changes and practical constraints. The diagrams remain valid as conceptual designs; the notes below document what changed and why.

\subsection*{Architectural Pivots}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Architectural Pivots --- Original vs Actual}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{LLL}
\toprule
\textbf{Diagram Element} & \textbf{Original Design} & \textbf{Actual Implementation} \\
\midrule
\textbf{RMRK 2.0 NFT Module} & All flows reference RMRK 2.0 as a participant & Replaced by \texttt{pallet-nfts} with attribute-based nesting \\
\textbf{XCM Scheduler} & Auto-renewal via scheduled XCM at block height & \texttt{on\_initialize} hook with \texttt{AutoRenewIndex} storage map \\
\textbf{Content Delivery Oracle} & PPV flow references an oracle for content streaming & Not implemented --- out of scope \\
\textbf{Royalty Distribution} & Revenue split and cross-chain distribution after each payment & \texttt{pay\_with\_royalties} distributes to up to 10 collaborators per payment \\
\textbf{Subscription Tiers} & Multiple tiers per content & Single subscription price per content \\
\textbf{Cross-Chain NFT Transfer} & Lock/mint wrapped ERC-721 on Ethereum via Snowbridge & Snowbridge v1 bridges fungible tokens (ETH), not NFTs \\
\textbf{Secondary Sale Royalties} & Bridge triggers royalty distribution on resale & Not implemented \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
}
\end{table}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{Architectural Pivots --- Rationale}
{\footnotesize
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{LL}
\toprule
\textbf{Diagram Element} & \textbf{Rationale for Change} \\
\midrule
\textbf{RMRK 2.0 NFT Module} & RMRK 2.0 pallets were abandoned by the community (frozen at polkadot-v0.9.36, incompatible with current polkadot-sdk) \\
\textbf{XCM Scheduler} & XCM v5 \texttt{Schedule} instruction is not production-ready; on-chain scheduler pattern achieves the same result \\
\textbf{Content Delivery Oracle} & Content delivery is an off-chain concern; the pallet manages access rights only \\
\textbf{Royalty Distribution} & Implemented for local collaborators; cross-chain royalty distribution via XCM is architecturally supported but not separately tested \\
\textbf{Subscription Tiers} & Simplified for thesis scope; multiple tiers could be added via separate content registrations \\
\textbf{Cross-Chain NFT Transfer} & NFT bridging requires Snowbridge v2 \texttt{Transact}; documented as future work \\
\textbf{Secondary Sale Royalties} & Requires marketplace integration and event-driven bridge callbacks \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
}
\end{table}

\subsection*{What Was Added Beyond the Original Design}

\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{\texttt{pallet-rights-verifier}} --- Merkle storage proof verification for trustless cross-chain rights checking (not in original diagrams)
    \item \textbf{Custom pallet-revive precompile} --- Efficient contract-to-pallet bridge for \texttt{check\_access} (not in original diagrams)
    \item \textbf{Full Snowbridge v1 E2E} --- Complete Ethereum $\rightarrow$ Bridge Hub $\rightarrow$ AssetHub token bridge with beacon light client, relayers, and proof verification (exceeded the original ``mock bridge'' scope)
    \item \textbf{\texttt{RightsMetadata} struct} --- Rich metadata emitted via events for cross-chain consumption, addressing Concept \#4
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{State Diagram Accuracy}

The Unified Rights Token State Diagram (Section 4) remains conceptually accurate. All states and transitions are implemented in \texttt{pallet-content-rights}:
\begin{itemize}
    \item ContentRegistered $\rightarrow$ SubscriptionActive/PPVAvailable/Owned: Complete
    \item SubscriptionActive $\rightarrow$ SubscriptionExpired (with auto-renewal): Complete
    \item PPVAvailable $\rightarrow$ PPVExhausted: Complete
    \item Owned $\rightarrow$ OwnedBridged: Partially (token bridging only, not NFT bridging)
\end{itemize}

